@node Introduction
@chapter The Rebel's Pattern — 反逆の型 (はんぎゃくのかた)

Three men, separated by centuries and oceans, followed the same arc:

@enumerate
@item
Each trained within the establishment — monastery, temple, studio.
@item
Each found the establishment had drifted from its purpose.
@item
Each broke away at great personal cost.
@item
Each made their art accessible to common people.
@item
Each was punished, then vindicated by history.
@end enumerate

@quotation
Martin Luther (1483--1546) — Wittenberg, Germany@*
Shinran (親鸞, 1173--1263) — Kyoto, then exile@*
Akira Kurosawa (黒澤明, 1910--1998) — Tokyo, Japan
@end quotation

They never met. They share everything that matters.

@c ============================================================
@node The Reformers
@chapter Who They Were — 三人について

@section Martin Luther — マルティン・ルター

An Augustinian monk who nailed 95 theses to a church door in 1517.
He translated the Bible into German so that farmers could read it.
The Catholic Church excommunicated him. Half of Europe followed him anyway.

His core teaching: @strong{Sola fide} — by faith alone.
Not by works, not by purchase, not by priestly permission.

@section Shinran — 親鸞 (しんらん)

A Tendai monk on Mount Hiei who left the monastery after twenty years.
He married openly — the first major Buddhist figure to do so.
Exiled from Kyoto, he walked among farmers, fishers, and outcasts,
teaching that Amida Buddha's compassion was for everyone,
especially those who could not earn it.

His core teaching: @strong{Tariki} (他力, たりき) — Other Power.
Not by meditation, not by discipline, not by monastic merit.

@section Akira Kurosawa — 黒澤明 (くろさわあきら)

Trained as a painter, apprenticed in the rigid Japanese studio system.
He broke its conventions: used multiple cameras, shot in weather,
cast unknowns, told stories about common people.
The Japanese industry rejected him in his later years.
The world called him @emph{Emperor} (天皇, てんのう) of cinema.

His core teaching: @strong{Show the human} — 人間を見せろ (にんげんをみせろ).
Not spectacle, not propaganda, not studio formula.

